​ Quickstart 
1 Get a Braintrust API key Create a Braintrust API key and set it as an environment variable: export BRAINTRUST_API_KEY = &quot;&lt;your-braintrust-api-key&gt;&quot; 
Gateway requests use the permissions of the user or service account that owns the key. To use an organization-level provider , the owner needs Read access to that provider. To use a project-level provider , the owner needs Read access to the project. If the Gateway denies a request because the provider is unavailable, confirm that the owner has the required Read access. 2 Add your AI provider key Add your provider API key in Braintrust so the Gateway can call it on your behalf — you won’t need to set your provider key locally. You can do this at the organization level (available across all projects) or the project level (overrides organization defaults). See how Braintrust chooses a provider for the rules that decide which provider a request uses. 3 Point your SDK at the Gateway Change your SDK’s base URL to https://gateway.braintrust.dev and pass your Braintrust API key as the API key. That’s it — no other code changes needed. https://gateway.braintrust.dev is the global hosted Gateway endpoint. It uses DNS latency routing and health checks across Braintrust-hosted Gateway regions. Gateway routing is separate from your organization’s data plane region . When logging is enabled , Gateway logs are written to your organization’s configured data plane. OpenAI Anthropic Gemini cURL Set the base URL to https://gateway.braintrust.dev . TypeScript import { OpenAI } from &quot;openai&quot; ; 

